#AREA Festival~

#AUTHORS Mag~

#HELPS
-1 FESTIVAL_CHANGES~
03.17.09 - Corrected an issue with the ghost.  He now junks the sheet
           received from players. (Order)

~
-1 FESTIVAL~
FESTIVAL
The festival was once a major attraction in the realms.  It drew
visitors from all over.  It was handed down through the generations
from father to son but has suffered greatly from a lack of attention.
The current manager seems to have inherited more than he can handle.
Stop by the festival, buy a ticket, and see if you can lend a hand.
~
0 $~

#RANGES 35 55 0 99

#FLAGS AFLAG_NODEBUG

#MOBILES

#37201
manager~
The manager~
The festival manager stands beside a large mahogany desk.~
The festival manager is a huge man.  He looks as though he is at least
7 feet tall.  He has a very worried look on his face.  What could be
bothering him?~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE|ACT_NO_ORDER
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_UNDERSTAND|AFF_TONGUES
100 S
93 BODY_ARM|BODY_HAND BODY_ARM|BODY_HAND 1d1+18908 3d10+60
500 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>greet_prog 100~
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 4
    if quest (4,3,$n) == 5
      if quest (15,3,$n) == 4
        say Come with me.
        say I found something for you earlier.
        mpecho The manager grabs some items from the safe and takes
        mpecho you into a small room in the back of his office.
        mptransfer $n 37337
        mpgoto 37337
        say There is a young lady that works in the ticket booth.
        say She is quite the artist.
        say She took items dropped by the animals in the exhibits
        say From them she made these things.
        say She took them to Verona and had them enchanted so they
        say would be as powerful as they are beautiful.
        say I think she would agree that you have earned them.
        mpoload 37306
        give i37306 $n
        mpoload 37307
        give i37307 $n
        mpoload 37308
        give i37308 $n
        mpoload 37309
        give i37309 $n
        mpoload 37310
        give i37310 $n
        mpmset $n quest 0 3 3
        mpmset $n quest 11 3 5
        say When you are ready to leave let me know.
        say Just say leave but you won't be able to come back here
        say so make sure you get everything.
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 3
    say My employee tells me he is very happy
    say with the sheet you gave him.
    say Thank you very much.
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 4
  endif
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 4
    say Good job getting rid of the Illusionist.
    say Who would have believed he would fall in
    say love with a wax statue.
    mpmset $n quest 4 3 5
  endif
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 0
    sigh
    emote lowers his head and mutters to himself
    say When my father left me this festival I had
    say no idea the problems I was in for.
  endif
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 1
    say You never answered me before.
    say You think you can help me?
  endif
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
    say Shouldn't you be out getting some of
    say those projects done?
  endif
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 3
    say Thank you for finishing up those tasks.
    say Things are sure to be better around here from now on.
  endif
~
>speech_prog leave~
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 5
    mpecho The manager escorts you back into his office.
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 6
    mptransfer $n 37368
    mppurge $i 
~
>speech_prog problems~
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 0
    emote raises his head and looks at $n
    say What are my problems?  What problems don't I
    say have would be a better question.
    sigh
    say I have an illusionist that thinks he owns
    say the House of Mirrors, a ghost that couldn't
    say maintain a uniform if his life depended on
    say it and then there are my finances.
    say I could really use some help.
    say You think you are up to the task?
    mpmset $n quest 0 3 1
  endif
~
>speech_prog yes~
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 1
    mpmset $n quest 20 2 1
    say I guess we'll just take one step at a time.
    say Would you like to hear about the ghost, the
    say illusionist or my finances?
    mpmset $n quest 0 3 2
  endif
~
>speech_prog no~
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 1
    say I'm sorry to hear that.
    say I'd appreciate it if you would leave me alone.
    mpmset $n quest 20 2 2
    emote pushes you quickly out of his office.
    mpmset $n quest 0 3 0
    mptransfer pcs 37202
  endif
~
>speech_prog illusionist~
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
    say There is an illusionist who has set himself up
    say in the House of Mirrors.  I have tried sending
    say people in to remove him but they haven't been
    say able to get to him.  I even tried those guys
    say from Hero for Hire.  All they did was run like
    say cowards.  If you could get rid of him for me
    say I'd appreciate it.
    mpmset $n quest 4 3 1
  endif
~
>speech_prog ghost~
  if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
    say One of my employees, the one who plays the
    say ghost in the Haunted House, has a problem with
    say his costume.  Every day he shows up for work in
    say sheets that are filthy and full of holes.  I've
    say sent his sheets to Lottie's in Chakkor to get
    say them cleaned.  I've given him every sheet I
    say could find but still he comes to work in dirty
    say sheets.  Maybe you could talk to him and see
    say if you can take care of the problem.
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 1
  endif
~
>speech_prog finances~
  if quest (15,3,$n) == 0
    if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
      say The carnival is having serious financial
      say problems.  The Old Trusty Bank of Refuge Tribe
      say has threatened foreclosure.  My last chance to
      say appease them is to show them that the festival
      say donates time and resources to the local area.
      say Somewhere I had a letter from the Dwarven Day
      say Care thanking us for giving them a reduced
      say rate one day each year.  If I could find that
      say letter maybe I could get the bank off my back.
      mpmset $n quest 15 3 1
    endif
  endif
~
>give_prog i37259~
  if quest (15,3,$n) == 3
    mpmset self quest 0 4 1
    emote begins to read over the letter.
  endif
~
>rand_prog 100~
  if quest (0,4,self) == 3
    mpecho A short man comes running into the room.
    mpecho The manager leans down and gives some instructions to the courier.
    mpecho The manager gives the letter to the courier and hurries him from the room.
    mpjunk i37259
    say Thanks again for finding that letter.
    if quest (4,3,$n) < 4
      if quest (11,3,$n) < 3
        say You should probably get back to work.
      endif
    endif
    mpmset self quest 0 4 0
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 2
    mpecho {130}The manager shouts 'Sarah! Send in the courier.'{020}
    mpmset self quest 0 4 3
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 1
    say Thank you so much.
    say Maybe this will be enough for the banker.
    say I'll have it rushed to him immediately.
    mpmset $n quest 15 3 4
    mpmset self quest 0 4 2
  endif  
~
|    

#37202
unicorn~
the Unicorn~
The Unicorn herself is standing only a short distance away!~
You have been graced by the very rare chance of seeing the Unicorn itself.
The Unicorn is a beautiful creature that resembles a horse only vaguely. It
is delicate looking, with cloven hooves and a golden spiraling horn upon its
head. The green bejeweled eyes seem to be looking into your very soul. You 
would never dream of attacking this beautiful creature that is the very
embodiment of order and reason.~
