#37231
maracales illusionist~
Maracales~
Maracales the Illusionist lies in a small cot.~
You look at the old man.  He lies in a small cot covered by the brightest
sheet you have ever seen.  It almost hurts your eyes to look at him.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_RACE|ACT_SMART
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN
0 S
103 BODY_HEAD BODY_HEAD 1d1+11000 1d10+148
0 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>greet_prog 100~
  if quest (4,3,$n) < 1
    say You have wandered into a place you don't belong.
    say You have no purpose for being here and I won't be bothered
    say by foolish mortals.
    say When you have a reason to speak with me I'll be here.
    say Return then, if my pets will allow it, and I might find
    say you worthy of my attention.
    mptransfer pcs 37329
  endif
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 2
    say You still haven't answered me.  Will you be a friend or foe?
  endif
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 1
    say The foolish manager has sent more mortals to try to make me
    say leave?  When will he learn?
    emote look at $n
    say Somehow you seem different.  Perhaps you might be of use to
    say me.  I offer you a choice.  I have a task I must complete
    say before I leave this place.  You can either help me with this
    say or I can banish you from my presence as I have so many before.
    say Which will you be?  Friend or foe?
    mpmset $n quest 4 3 2
  endif
~
>speech_prog foe~
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 2
    say Very well.  I am a very busy man and do not have time to waste
    say on you.  If you should change your mind you know where to find
    say me.  I will leave word with my pets to send you to me if you
    say return.  Do not expect this courtesy to be extended for long.
    mpmset $n quest 7 3 5
    mptransfer pcs 37329
  endif
~
>speech_prog friend~
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 2
    say Good, let me tell you of how I came to be here.
    say Long ago I came to this festival in search of steady work.
    say This was as close as I could be to my beautiful wife and still
    say provide for her.  The festival manager gave me a job.  He paid
    say me room, board, and a small amount of money that I sent home
    say to my wife.  I did not have the money to visit her often.  He
    say seemed to like the idea that I could not leave.
    cough
    mpecho When Maracales coughs you notice several droplets of blood spatter on the sheet.
    mpecho The sheet instantly absorbs the drops and is as clean as ever.
    say One day I received word she was ill and I went to him and told
    say him I would be leaving to be with her.  Instead, he had her
    say brought to the festival to live and had his doctors help her.
    say The doctors couldn't help and one day her torment was ended.
    say I rushed to be with her but when I arrived at our tent I was
    say shocked to find that her body had been removed.  The manager
    say thought I would take this opportunity to leave and he used her
    say body to prevent it.  He underestimated my powers and my love
    say for my wife.  I vowed to find my wife's body and return it
    say home to be buried.  I took up residence in this building and
    say from here I use magic to search for her body.  Unfortunately,
    say I am unable to leave this building and that is where you can
    say help me.  I acquired a key that allows access to my wife's
    say resting place.  I do not know where that is but if you can
    say find and bring her to me I would gladly leave this prison.
    say Please hurry, this nightmare must end.
    say Farewell $n
    mpmset $n quest 7 3 5
    mpoload 37293
    give mechanickey $n
    mpmset $n quest 4 3 3
    mptransfer pcs 37329
  endif
~
>give_prog i37290~
  if quest (4,3,$n) == 3
    gasp
    mpecho Maracales springs from the cot, throwing the sparkling white
    mpecho sheet to the floor.
    mpecho {130}Maracales shouts 'I can't believe you did it!'{020}
    say I mean I hoped you would but I never dreamed.
    say At last I can take my one true love to her home.
    mpoload 37291
    drop sheet
    say I can't thank you enough for returning my wife.
    say Now, as we agreed I shall leave this horrid place.
    mpoload 37294
    mpecho Maracales searches his pockets until he finds a small key.
    mpecho He unlocks the door to the north, opens it and runs through.
    mpecho The door key falls to the floor as he leaves the room.
    drop waveringkey
    mpmset $n quest 7 3 0
    mpmset $n quest 4 3 4
    mppurge $i
~ 
|

#37232
ghost~
The ghost~
A festival employee covered in a dirty sheet stands here.~
This festival employee does his best to scare you but it just isn't working.
The thought of what diseases you might catch if you touch him scares you more
than his act.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_RACE|ACT_SMART
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN
0 S
103 BODY_HEAD BODY_HEAD 1d1+11000 1d100+88
0 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>greet_prog 100~
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 2
    say Any luck with my problem?
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 1
    emote raises his arms and waves them as he paces back and forth.
    mpecho {130}BooOOooOO!!{020}
    say The manager said you might be coming to see me.
    say I don't know what his problem is.  I do my best to
    say keep my stuff clean.  You know how hard it is to...
    emote reaches into his sheet and pulls out a sandwich.
    emote takes a large bite out of the biggest sandwich you've ever seen.
    say Sorry about that.  Scaring people is hungry work.
    say Anyway, you know how hard it is to keep sheets clean
    say around here?  Well let me tell you, it is impossible.
    mpecho As you listen to him speak you notice a blob of mustard on his chin.
    mpecho The mustard falls and lands on his sheet.
    sigh
    say This place is so dirty.  If that manager would get me a sheet
    say that didn't attract dust so much I'd be fine.  Oh well, it
    say just isn't meant to be.  Go away and leave me alone.  The 
    say manager is just going to have to get used to the fact that not
    say all ghosts wear sparkling white sheets.
    mpecho The ghost returns to his duties.
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 2
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 3
    say Thanks again for getting me that sheet.
    say I can't wait to try it out.
  endif
~
>rand_prog 15~
  emote raises his arms and waves them as he paces back and forth.
  mpecho {130}BooOOooOO!!{020}
~
>give_prog i37291~
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 3
      say But you've already given me a sheet.
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 2
    say Wow!
    say Thanks!
    say This is that crazy illusionist's sheet isn't it?
    say The one in the House of Mirrors.  I've seen it in his tent.
    say He once told me that it is stain proof and mends itself.  He
    say said it was a gift from his wife.  Apparently with him being
    say away from home she thought it would be great if he never had
    say to worry about fresh linens.  It is really great that he
    say would give this to me.  I'll have a clean costume from now on.
    mpjunk i37291
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 3
  
  endif
~
>give_prog i29841~
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 3
    say But you've already given me a sheet.
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) == 2
    say Wow!
    say Thanks!
    say I haven't seen a sheet this white since my days in ghost
    say training school in the House of Horrors.  Hey, this is
    say one of their sheets.  It must have been hard to get this
    say they don't give these away to just anyone.
    say I'll never forget what you've done for me.
    say I'll wear this next time I work.
    mpjunk i29841
    mpmset $n quest 11 3 3
  endif
~
|

#37233
repairman~
The festival repairman~
A repairman kneels working behind the crypt.~
This festival employee spends his day responding to the many mechanical
emergencies that arise.  He is covered in grease and grime from head to
foot.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_RACE|ACT_SMART
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN
0 S
103 BODY_HEAD BODY_HEAD 1d1+11000 1d10+148
0 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>greet_prog 100~
  mpecho The festival repairman raises up from behind the crypt when you enter.
  say Sorry folks, this exhibit is closed for repairs.
  mpecho The repairman kneels down behind the crypt and returns to his work.
~
>give_prog i37293~
  say Where did you get this key?
  say Never mind, it doesn't matter.
  say This is the key I've been looking for.
  say Now watch this.
  mpmset self quest 0 4 1
~
>rand_prog 100~
  if quest (0,4,self) == 5
    mpecho The repairman closes the crypt, locks the mechanism and hurries from the room.
    mpecho A small key falls from the repairman's pocket as he leaves the room.
    drop mechanickey
    mpmset self quest 0 4 0
    mppurge $i
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 4 
    say Oh well, I need to get back to work.
    mpmset self quest 0 4 5
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 3
    say That is so beautiful.
    say It chokes me up every time I see it.
    mpmset self quest 0 4 4
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 2
    mpecho The crypt opens and you see a wax carving of a beautiful woman.
    mpmset self quest 0 4 3
  endif
  if quest (0,4,self) == 1
    mpecho The repairman puts the key in the lock and turns.
    mpmset self quest 0 4 2
  endif  
~
|

#37234
small rat~
a small rat~
A small rat with extremely large, sharp teeth is crouching in the corner here.~
This small rat is backed into the corner and looks very mean.  You better hope
he doesn't have friends.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_AGGRESSIVE
AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN|AFF_DETECT_INVIS
-500 S
13 0 0 2d6+260 2d6+7
1495 3616
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>death_prog 100~
  mpecho The dying rat squeals loudly and another appears from a crack in the wall.
  mpmload 37234
~
|

#37235
Verona gypsy~
Verona~
Verona the gypsy is seated behind a small table.~
Verona is a rather small lady.  She is old and wrinkled but you get the
feeling that she has a deep understanding of all things past, present
and future.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_RACE|ACT_SMART
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN|AFF_SANCTUARY
0 S
103 BODY_HEAD BODY_HEAD 1d1+13436 1d100+148
0 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_FEMALE
>greet_prog 100~
  tell $n Hello my young friend.
  tell $n To find the future you must know the past.
  tell $n I can guide your future or reveal your past.
  tell $n Would you be interested?
  mpmset self quest 0 1 1
~
>speech_prog no~
  if quest (0,1,self) == 1
    sigh
    say Young people could learn so much if they would only try.
    sigh
    say We have nothing else to speak of my child.
    mpmset self quest 0 1 0
  endif
~
>speech_prog yes~
  if quest (0,1,self) == 1
    mpmset self quest 0 1 0
    mpmset self quest 1 1 1
    tell $n Very good, let's go to a more private place. 
    mptransfer $n 37335
    mpgoto 37335
    emote ushers you to a quiet room in the back of the booth.
    mpforce $n look
    tell $n If at any time you wish to leave just say so.
    tell $n I do not want to make you uncomfortable.
    tell $n I am a seer of both past and future.  Which interests you?
  endif
~    
>speech_prog leave~
  if quest (1,1,self) == 1
  mpmset self quest 1 1 0
  emote quickly leads you back to the front of the booth.
  mptransfer $n 37365
  mpgoto 37365
  tell $n I have returned you to my booth.
~
>speech_prog past~
  if quest (1,1,self) == 1
    if quest (0,3,$n) < 1
      tell $n Your past is cloudy to me.
    endif
    if quest (0,3,$n) > 0
      tell $n I see the manager telling you of his problems.
      if quest (0,3,$n) < 2
        if quest (20,,$n) == 0
          tell $n I see him asking you for assistance but you do not answer.
          tell $n I am sorry friend but the rest of your past is hidden.
        endif
      endif
      if quest (20,1,$n) == 1
        tell $n It is good that you agreed to help him.
        if quest (15,3,$n) < 1
          if quest (11,3,$n) < 1
            if quest (4,3,$n) < 1
              tell $n I am sorry young friend but the rest of your past is hidden.
            endif
          endif
        endif
      endif
      endif
      if quest (20,1,$n) == 2
        tell $n I see you telling the manager you wouldn't help him.
        tell $n I am sorry friend but the rest of your past is hidden.
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if quest (15,3,$n) > 0
    tell $n I see the manager told you of his problems with the bank.
    tell $n He said a letter can help him avoid foreclosure.
    tell $n The letter was written by someone from the Dwarven Day Care.
    if quest (15,3,$n) < 2
      tell $n This matter remains a problem for the manager.
    endif
    if quest (15,3,$n) > 3
      tell $n I see you found the letter and returned it to the manager.
      tell $n He dispatched a courier to take the letter to the bank.
      tell $n You cannot help further with this matter.
    endif
  endif
  if quest (11,3,$n) > 0
    tell $n I see the manager told you of the ghost's uniform problems.
    if quest (11,3,$n) < 2
      tell $n This matter remains a problem for the manager.
    endif
    if quest (11,3,$n) > 1
      tell $n I see you and the ghost talking.
      tell $n He told you he cannot keep a sheet clean in this place.
      if quest (11,3,$n) < 3
        tell $n This matter remains a problem for the manager.
      endif
      if quest (11,3,$n) > 2
        tell $n I see you giving the ghost a beautiful white sheet.
        if quest (11,3,$n) > 3
          tell $n I see the manager congratulating you on helping the ghost.
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if quest (4,3,$n) > 0
    tell $n The manager told you he his problems with an illusionist.
    if quest (4,3,$n) > 2
      tell $n I see you speaking with Maracales.
      tell $n He talks of his wife's body and asks you to help find it.
      if quest (4,3,$n) > 3
        tell $n He accepts the wax statue you give him and leaves.
        if quest (4,3,$n) > 4
          tell $n The manager thanks you for helping rid him of Maracales.
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if quest (0,3,$n) > 3
    tell $n You have done all the manager has asked.
  endif
~
>speech_prog future~
  if quest (1,1,self) == 1
    emote searches the future in the depths of the crystal ball.
    if quest (20,2,$n) > 1
      tell $n The manager asked for your help.
      tell $n Good things come to those who help others.
    endif
    if quest (0,3,$n) < 1
      tell $n You must return to the manager and ask of his problems.
    endif
    if quest (0,3,$n) == 1
      tell $n The manager needs your help and awaits your answer.
    endif
    if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
      tell $n The manager told you of his problems,
      tell $n He has problems with finances, a ghost, and an illusionist.
      tell $n Let us see what you should do.
    endif
    if quest (15,3,$n) == 0
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n You must know the problem before you find the answer.
        tell $n Learn more of the manager's finances.
      endif
    endif   
    if quest (15,3,$n) == 1
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n The manager told you of the letter.
        tell $n The manager needs that letter to save the festival.
        tell $n Perhaps you should search places he might have been.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (11,3,$n) == 0
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n You have yet to hear the story of the ghost.
        tell $n I suspect the manager would be glad to share.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (11,3,$n) == 1
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n Seek out the ghost for he too has a story.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (11,3,$n) == 2
      if quest (0,3,$n) ==2
        tell $n You must help the ghost with his sheet problems.
        tell $n Perhaps you could find him a new one.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (11,3,$n) == 3
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n You have given the ghost a beautiful new sheet.
        tell $n You should make certain the manager knows.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (4,3,$n) == 0
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2
        tell $n The manager waits to tell you of the illusionist.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (4,3,$n) == 1
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2       
        tell $n The manager told you of the illusionist.
        tell $n But there are two sides to every story.
      endif
    endif
    if quest (4,3,$n) == 3
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2         
        tell $n The illusionist told you the story of his wife.
        tell $n But have you found her and given her to him?
      endif
    endif
    if quest (4,3,$n) == 4
      if quest (0,3,$n) == 2  
        tell $n You have returned the illusionist's wife.
        tell $n But does the manager know yet?
      endif
    endif
    if quest (4,3,$n) > 4
      if quest (11,3,$n) > 3
        if quest (15,3,$n) > 3
          if quest (0,3,$n) < 3
            tell $n You have helped the manager all you can.
            tell $n Perhaps he has a reward for you.
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endif
    if quest (0,3,$n) > 2
      tell $n I see nothing here for you in the future.
      tell $n You have done all you can do.
    endif
  endif    
~
|

