This booth is divided by posts and chains into several aisles.  Each aisle
ends at a small mirror with a slot in the bottom.  As you get closer you
realize there are people on the other side of the mirrors waiting to sell
you tickets to the festival.~
372 ROOM_INDOORS|ROOM_SAFE SECT_INSIDE
DDIR_EAST
You see an open area marking the entrance to the festival.~
~
0 -1 37202
E
mirror~
There are three fingerprint stained mirrors on the wall here.  Maybe on the
wall isn't the best way to describe it.  In the wall would be better.  When
you look into one of the mirrors you think you see people standing behind
them.  But mainly you just see the face of some poor soul staring back at
you.  Oh, never mind, that's just your reflection.
~
E
posts~
The posts here are sunk into the ground to form a sort of barrier.
~
E
chains~
The chains are hung between the posts in such a way that they guide people
to one of the three windows.  They are a bit rusty and should probably be
replaced.
~
S

#37368
Festival manager's office~
This very clean office holds a large desk, a safe, and a chair.  Judging
by the size of the desk, the person that sits here is very large.  Judging
by the size of the safe, the amount of money kept here is very small.~
372 ROOM_INDOORS|ROOM_SAFE|ROOM_PRIVATE SECT_INSIDE
DDIR_WEST
You see an open area marking the entrance to the festival.~
~
